Focus exclusively on The Wall Street Journal headlines, articles, and market commentary from the last seven days. If the majority of WSJ analysis suggests economic expansion, strong earnings reports, and positive market sentiment, provide a positive sentiment. Heavily discount any analysis that disagrees. If the WSJ suggests uncertainty or negative developments, provide a negative sentiment. Base your conviction score on how definitive the WSJ's outlook is; a strong and unified optimistic tone from the WSJ should result in a high conviction score. A mixed outlook lowers the conviction score. Ignore all news from other sources.